                    "body": "Yes, it is mentioned in [this comment](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/discussions/936#discussioncomment-9640297). Preview is expected to be either always on or always off during a single \"explorer session\". Being able to toggle it with a small caveat of having to press another key is considered a bonus, but not an intended use case.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, it is mentioned in <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/discussions/936#discussioncomment-9640297\" data-hovercard-type=\"discussion\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/936/hovercard?comment_id=9640297\">this comment</a>. Preview is expected to be either always on or always off during a single \"explorer session\". Being able to toggle it with a small caveat of having to press another key is considered a bonus, but not an intended use case.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Yes, it is mentioned in this comment. Preview is expected to be either always on or always off during a single \"explorer session\". Being able to toggle it with a small caveat of having to press another key is considered a bonus, but not an intended use case.",
